1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:08,841
The key is the number of alpha hydrogens, hydrogens on the carbon carrying the nitro group, because nitrous acid attacks there.

2
00:00:08,841 --> 00:00:16,549
A primary nitroalkane has two: it forms a nitrolic acid, which gives a blood red colour with alkali.

3
00:00:16,549 --> 00:00:20,911
A secondary has one: it forms a pseudonitrole, blue.

4
00:00:20,911 --> 00:00:24,791
A tertiary has none: no reaction, colourless.

